@startuml
title One round of KECCAK-p[1600, 24], repeated for round index 0 to 23
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

start
:State array A, 5 x 5 x 64 bits\nA[x,y,z] = S[64(5y + x) + z];
repeat :theta\nXOR each bit with the parity of the\ncolumn at x-1 and the column at x+1\nshifted by one in z  (linear diffusion);
  :rho\nrotate each of the 25 lanes by a fixed\noffset depending on its (x, y);
  :pi\npermute lane positions:\nA'[x,y,z] = A[(x + 3y) mod 5, x, z];
  :chi\nper 5-bit row: a ^= (~b) & c\n(the only non-linear step, degree 2);
  :iota\nXOR the round constant into lane (0,0),\nbreaking symmetry between rounds;
repeat while (round index < 24) is (yes)
->no;
:Permuted 1600-bit state;
stop

note right
  XOR, AND, NOT and rotation only.
  No lookup tables, no data-dependent
  branches, so the permutation is
  constant-time by construction.
end note
@enduml
